{
  "id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/esquisto",
  "type": "Concept",
  "prefLabel": {
    "es": "esquisto",
    "en": "schist"
  },
  "definition": {
    "es": "Roca metamórfica fanerítica y foliada que presenta una esquistosidad muy desarrollada y continua, lo que implica que más del 50 por ciento del volumen de la roca son granos minerales con hábito tabular, lamelar o prismático acicular, orientados en una fábrica continua planar o lineal.",
    "en": "Foliated phaneritic metamorphic rock with well developed, continuous schistosity, meaning that greater than 50 percent of the rock by volume is mineral grains with a thin tabular, lamellar, or acicular prismatic crystallographic habit that are oriented in a continuous planar or linear fabric."
  },
  "narrower": [
    {
      "id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/micaesquisto",
      "prefLabel": {
        "es": "micaesquisto",
        "en": "mica schist"
      }
    }
  ],
